CORE no-new-smt broken-smt-backend wide-pointer-encoding
main.c
--wide-pointer-encoding
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] .* assertion ptr != x: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Issue #8200: with wide pointer encoding, a constant integer cast to
a pointer can equal a string literal's address. The address-based
pointer equality detects this.
